From 4f078a227bb8ea97870c7adc57c944bbc519c9c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Reed <reedswork@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:21:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] client: optional Chrome-shaped ClientHello
 (ClientConfig::chrome_hello)

Chrome's cipher suite list and order, GREASE in the cipher suites,
extensions, groups, key shares, versions and signature algorithms, the
extensions BoringSSL adds for Chrome (signed_certificate_timestamp,
renegotiation_info instead of the SCSV, ALPS for h2 answered with the
client's EncryptedExtensions when the server takes it, a GREASE
encrypted_client_hello, trust_anchors), random extension order between a
leading empty and a trailing one-byte GREASE extension, the PSK offer last.
Certificate entries may carry the SCTs and trust anchor answers this asks
for; they are skipped.
---
